e_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n**Reproducible in** \n- Reproducible in: v4.7.rc1.mono.official [a4f5e8cdd]\n- Reproducible in: Lastest master (v4.7.rc.gh [ec67cbe92])\n\n**Not Reproducible**\n- Not Reproducible in: v4.6.2.stable.mono.official [71f334935]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.rc (ec67cbe92) - Windows 10 (build 17134) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1070 (NVIDIA; 31.0.15.3141) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-7700 CPU @ 3.60GHz (8 threads) - 23.92 GiB memory - WASAPI (96000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe `GPUParticle3D` shows up completely broken after adding the process material. \nSometimes it shows the particle totally distorted as if the basis is broken, sometimes the particle does not spawn correctly at all.\n\nReloading the saved scene seems to fix this issue. This only happens when the node is created the first time.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a538c771-4c40-44f4-900a-8bc657f7c641\n\nHere is the whole process. This time, the basis seems to be broken:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9145c0d7-227b-417c-83f8-3bb85acb8a23\n\nHere is it working on 4.6 like it should:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/449fbb87-6d3b-4385-a0b5-310f93f02b5f\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Add a GPUParticle3D\n- Add a draw pass BoxMesh\n- Add a process material\nResult: Particle is broken. Either not moving with the GPUParticle3D node, or distorted\n\nExpected result: Particle working normally\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNot needed, any empty scene can reproduce this.","closed_by":{"login":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieSha